From 3b7cb294af4f67ef506e34fac006fd97290d8e90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tonka <tonkatriathlete@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 01:42:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hermes-agent): scope anchor to rep + always report failed
 runs

Two correctness fixes on nearby_prospect:

- getEvents now accepts repId and forwards it as a query param, so the
  anchor is the rep's own most recent visit rather than any rep's last
  visit (multi-rep correctness bug).
- runNearbyProspect now wraps its core in a lifecycle: a thrown I/O error
  PATCHes the run status=failed (with the message) and rethrows, instead of
  leaving it stuck at "running". Run-status telemetry is routed through a
  best-effort reportRun helper, so a patchRun failure can no longer discard
  an otherwise-successful run.

Adds tests/nearby-prospect.test.ts: 6 orchestrator tests over a real
HermesClient with injected fetch (repId in events query, failed-on-throw,
resilient telemetry, completed/skipped paths). Suite now 21 tests, all pass.
